    "created_at": "2016-01-04T13:23:59Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-04T13:23:59Z",
    "body": "I tried to figure out a plan, but it's unclear to me what is best. Clearly it would be better if some of the API-level requirements became network-requirements instead, but currently we have no control over the network. Perhaps maintaining a (big) monkey patch in HTML is the way to go? Figuring out if we can reuse Fetch in some fashion also still seems attractive, since duplicating all the requirements is kind of cumbersome.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
